    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d279">

                <pb facs="0803" n="770" sameAs="frus:frus1969-76v24/pg770"/>

                <head>279. Telegram From the Department of State to the
                        Embassy in Jordan<anchor n="1" xml:id="d279-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>Washington</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1970-09-20T22:35:00+00:00">September 20, 1970,
                        2235Z</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>154431. 1. The British Ambassador has called urgently to state that his
                    understanding of appeal which King has made to HMG is that UK
                    <pb facs="0804" n="771" xml:id="pg771"/> undertake airstrike against invading
                    Syrian forces.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d279-f2"/> From your reporting we had not
                    repeat not been aware that King had made such request of British nor is it clear
                    that King in his appeal to us for USG
                        assistance<anchor n="3" xml:id="d279-f3"/> had specifically in mind a US airstrike.</p>
                <p>2. Please clarify this urgently.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#bold">Rogers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d279-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d279-f1-content">
                <p>Source: National Archives, RG 59, Central Files
                    1970–73, POL 23–9 JORDAN. Secret; Flash; Exdis. Drafted and approved by Seelye. It was repeated Flash to London.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f2" n="2" xml:id="d279-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 7568 from London, September 20, 1242Z, reported that the King contacted
                    the British Embassy in Amman to request assistance. (Ibid., Nixon Presidential Materials, NSC Files, Box 619, Country Files, Middle East,
                    Jordan Crisis)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d279-f3" n="3" xml:id="d279-f3-content">
                <p>Reported in telegram 4951 from Amman, September 20, 0720Z. (Ibid., RG 59, Central Files 1970–73, POL 23–9 JORDAN)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
